    "title": "Правила: Maybe vs May be – Grammar Shorts",
    "level": "SHORTS",
    "overview": "Maybe и may be звучат одинаково, но это разные грамматические конструкции.",
    "main_rule": "Maybe = adverb meaning perhaps. May be = modal may + verb be.",
    "form": "Maybe + clause. subject + may be + complement.",
    "when_why": "Если можно заменить на perhaps → maybe. Если modal + be является частью verb phrase → may be.",
    "examples": "Maybe she is busy. → Возможно, она занята.\nShe may be busy. → Возможно, она занята.\nMaybe we'll go tomorrow. → Может быть, мы поедем завтра.\nThey may be late. → Возможно, они опоздают.",
    "special_cases": "Position reveals structure: Maybe often stands at sentence level; may be is part of predicate.",
    "common_mistakes": "❌ She maybe busy. → ✅ She may be busy. / Maybe she is busy.\n❌ Maybe she may be busy. → Possible but changes emphasis; don't use one as a spelling variant of the other.",
    "dont_confuse": "maybe = perhaps.\nmay be = modal + be.",
    "quick_summary": "maybe = one word adverb.\nmay be = two-word verb phrase."
  },
